{"slug":"btc-led-weekly-momentum-on-eth-and-sol","name":"BTC-led weekly momentum on ETH and SOL","status":"rejected","created_at":"2026-11-13T08:44:36.989402Z","version":1,"frozen":true,"implementation":"btc-led-weekly","runs":3,"trials":3,"deflated_sharpe":0.0022476400281317144,"asset_class":"crypto","sections":{"hypothesis":"Hypothesis","rationale":"Why the edge should exist","rules":"Rules in plain English","falsification":"What would prove it wrong","parameters":"Parameters and allowed ranges","costs":"Expected turnover against costs"},"notes":[{"version":1,"created_at":"2026-11-13T08:44:36.989402Z","sections":{"hypothesis":"BTC leads and the large alts follow with a lag, so BTC's week predicts ETH's and SOL's next week: holding ETH or SOL for the week after BTC's Sunday-to-Sunday return was positive, and cash otherwise, beats holding the coin on risk-adjusted return after costs, and beats trading the coin on its own weekly return.","rationale":"Luke's idea: ETH and SOL move on BTC's moves, not the other way round. Lead-lag between large and small assets is a long-documented effect in equities (large stocks' returns lead small stocks'), and crypto's market is dominated by BTC. The idea was stated as a follow-up in the weekly-momentum-on-btc-followers note (rejected 2026-11-13), whose own-coin version cut drawdowns but didn't beat holding on ETH 2017-19 or SOL. Formed after seeing those results, so it is a new trial, tested on windows where the own-coin version has already been run, for a like-for-like comparison. Weak points: if BTC and ETH/SOL move together within the same day rather than with a lag, BTC's week adds nothing the coin's own week doesn't already show; SOL's 2020-25 period is the one the earlier idea was formed on; after about 155 trials, a pass is modest evidence. Expected odds: low.","rules":"Implementation btc-led-weekly. Daily bars of the traded coin, with BTCUSDT's close on the same bar attached (btc_close, matched by open time). At each Sunday's close (UTC), BTC's week is its close over its close exactly 7 days earlier (by date; a missing BTC close at either end means no signal, cash). Positive: hold the coin fully until the next Sunday's close; otherwise cash. Decide at the close, trade at the next open; 2% no-trade band; long only, spot; 10 bps fee, 1 bp half-spread, square-root impact.","falsification":"Three runs, once each, 330 USDT: ETHUSDT 1d 2017-08 to 2019-12; ETHUSDT 1d 2020-01 to 2025-10; SOLUSDT 1d 2020-08 to 2025-10. Reject unless, on all three: (1) Sharpe above buy-and-hold's; (2) total return beats the coin held at the strategy's average exposure; (3) max drawdown smaller than buy-and-hold's; (4) break-even cost at least twice the cost paid; (5) better Sharpe than holding from at least 60% of 1-year start dates. Mechanism, decided now: the lead-lag story is supported only if Sharpe is also above the coin's own weekly momentum on the same window in all three (runs 20261113-083106-e305a6 ETH 2017-19 Sharpe 0.13, 20261113-075823-b9bc01 ETH 2020-25 Sharpe 1.23, 20261113-083106-c0e1a0 SOL Sharpe 1.08). A pass moves it to Watch, not Pursue; the holdout (from 2025-11) stays untouched.","parameters":"None: one-week horizon, BTC as the leader.","costs":"About 15-25 round trips a year at about 22-26 bps each (SOL's spread is wider), 3-6% a year."},"implementation":"btc-led-weekly","frozen_at":"2026-11-13T08:44:36.991782Z","change_reason":null}],"history":[{"status":"idea","at":"2026-11-13T08:44:36.989402Z","reason":"Created"},{"status":"specified","at":"2026-11-13T08:44:36.991800Z","reason":"v1 frozen"},{"status":"backtested","at":"2026-11-13T08:44:57.754874Z","reason":"first run on v1"},{"status":"rejected","at":"2026-11-13T08:45:18.438533Z","reason":"Pre-registered test (runs 20261113-084457-8068a1 ETH 2017-19, 20261113-084458-e5610f ETH 2020-25, 20261113-084458-c3c7f4 SOL 2020-25). Failed rule 1 on all three: Sharpe 0.10 vs 0.15, 1.07 vs 1.12 and 1.08 vs 1.24 for holding; rule 5 on ETH 2017-19 (29%) and SOL (35%); rule 4 on ETH 2017-19 (break-even 0); rule 2 on ETH 2017-19 (-37% vs -15%) and SOL (+1,901% vs +2,047%). Passed rule 3 on all three (smaller drawdown). Mechanism not supported: BTC's week as the signal did no better than the coin's own week (0.10 vs 0.13, 1.07 vs 1.23, 1.08 vs 1.08), so in daily data the alts don't lag BTC by enough to trade at a weekly horizon."}],"trial_log":[{"id":"20261113-084457-8068a1","created_at":"2026-11-13T08:44:57.748725Z","strategy":"btc-led-weekly","strategy_kind":"research","style":"weights","engine":"event","params":{},"research":{"slug":"btc-led-weekly-momentum-on-eth-and-sol","version":1},"strategy_name":"ETHUSDT on BTC's weekly momentum","symbol":"ETHUSDT","benchmark_symbol":"ETHUSDT","universe_coins":null,"forced_exits":0,"deflated_sharpe":0.00036755337946270394,"deflated_trials":883,"interval":"1d","start":"2017-08","end":"2019-12","scored_from":null,"history_from":null,"initial_cash":"330.0","account_currency":"USDT","used_holdout":false,"config_fingerprint":"34297ef0cb6e","code":{"commit":"4e8c6c7c3ecedf9d8e1bce4021cad5f46785e571","dirty":false},"metrics":{"start":"2017-08-17T00:00:00Z","end":"2020-01-01T00:00:00Z","days":867,"final_equity":207.71824409959535,"total_return":-0.37055077545577164,"cagr":-0.17706775611576597,"volatility":0.7309333501141643,"sharpe":0.09922619165099983,"sharpe_ci":[-1.1725941530653223,1.371046536367322],"psr":0.5607671463327393,"sortino":0.14396721258305975,"max_drawdown":-0.8215632372706169,"longest_underwater_days":717.0,"skew":0.19816010689534141,"kurtosis":10.40879018345458,"exposure":0.5409237481816019,"trades":62,"rejections":0,"band_skips":0,"fees":21.915193579056464,"spread_costs":2.1915123470000006,"impact_costs":0.7042999743482029,"total_costs":24.811005900404666,"turnover":25.89085166657235,"few_trades":false,"round_trips":null,"win_rate":null,"avg_win_r":null,"avg_loss_r":null,"expectancy_r":null,"profit_factor":null,"avg_cost_r":null,"risk_capped":null},"benchmark_m